---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '~/consts';

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-11-09');
const dateFormatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', {
  month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric',
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles your data on this website. Short answer: as little as possible.`}
  canonical="/privacy"
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>How this site handles your data.</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {dateFormatter.format(lastUpdated)}</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Short answer: as little as possible. This page is longer only so it can
          be specific about <em>what</em> little.
        </p>

        <h2>What this site collects</h2>

        <p>
          This website uses <a href="https://aptabase.com" rel="noopener">Aptabase</a>
          for aggregate, anonymous analytics. We record:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Which page was visited (the path, not the query string)</li>
          <li>Approximate country and operating system</li>
          <li>Approximate time of visit</li>
          <li>Aggregate engagement signals: how far you scrolled on a page (as a 25 / 50 / 75 / 100 percent milestone), whether you finished reading a guide (reaching the 90 percent mark), and which outbound links you clicked (Play Store listings, our contact email, external sites). Link tracking records only the destination hostname, never the link text or any content you selected.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>We do not record:</p>

        <ul>
          <li>Your IP address (Aptabase hashes it and does not store it)</li>
          <li>Any identifier that could link visits across sessions</li>
          <li>Any cross-site tracking identifier</li>
          <li>Any personal information (we don't collect any)</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          No cookies are set by this website. No third-party trackers are loaded.
          No ad networks are present. If you block analytics entirely, the site
          works exactly the same.
        </p>

        <h2>What you send us directly</h2>

        <p>
          If you email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, we
          read your message, reply, and keep the thread in our inbox the same way
          anyone keeps an email thread. We don't add you to a mailing list and
          don't share the message with anyone else.
        </p>

        <h2>What the apps we build do</h2>

        <p>
          Each app has its own privacy policy (linked from the app's own
          documentation). This policy covers only the <em>website</em> you're
          currently on. The short version for our apps: we default to on-device,
          collect anonymous crash + usage telemetry only, and never link telemetry
          to a person.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share data with</h2>

        <p>No one. The only third party we use is Aptabase, our analytics provider,
          and only as described above. We don't sell data. We don't swap data with
          other companies. We don't run ad retargeting. There is nothing to sell;
          there is nothing to swap.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

        <p>
          If this policy changes materially, the Last updated date above changes
          with it. Earlier versions are preserved in our git history and available
          on request.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding: 5rem 0 3rem; }

  .container {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-gold-400);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 0.375rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-gold-500) 30%, transparent);
    border-radius: 100px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .updated {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-dim);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
